# 基础词 Unit14
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2025红宝书考研英语词汇
# 描述: 基础词Unit14核心词汇

{{pace}}{{/peɪs}}{{n./v. 步伐；速度；踱步}}{{The company is growing at a rapid pace.}}
{{pack}}{{/pæk}}{{v./n. 打包；一包}}{{She packed her suitcase for the trip.}}
{{pale}}{{/peɪl}}{{adj. 苍白的；浅色的}}{{She looked pale after the illness.}}
{{panel}}{{/ˈpænl}}{{n. 面板；专家组}}{{The expert panel discussed the issue at length.}}
{{panic}}{{/ˈpænɪk}}{{n./v. 恐慌；惊慌}}{{The fire caused panic among the shoppers.}}
{{parade}}{{/pəˈreɪd}}{{n./v. 游行；检阅}}{{The military parade was held on National Day.}}
{{parallel}}{{/ˈpærəlel}}{{adj./n. 平行的；相似之物}}{{The two roads run parallel to each other.}}
{{parcel}}{{/ˈpɑːsl}}{{n. 包裹}}{{She sent a parcel to her friend abroad.}}
{{pardon}}{{/ˈpɑːdn}}{{n./v. 原谅；赦免}}{{I beg your pardon; I didn't hear what you said.}}
{{partial}}{{/ˈpɑːʃl}}{{adj. 部分的；偏爱的}}{{The project is only a partial success.}}
{{participate}}{{/pɑːˈtɪsɪpeɪt}}{{v. 参加；参与}}{{All students are encouraged to participate in sports.}}
{{particular}}{{/pəˈtɪkjələr}}{{adj. 特定的；讲究的}}{{Is there a particular reason for your absence?}}
{{passion}}{{/ˈpæʃn}}{{n. 热情；激情}}{{She has a passion for music.}}
{{passive}}{{/ˈpæsɪv}}{{adj. 被动的；消极的}}{{He took a passive role in the discussion.}}
{{passport}}{{/ˈpɑːspɔːt}}{{n. 护照}}{{You need a valid passport to travel abroad.}}
{{paste}}{{/peɪst}}{{n./v. 糊；粘贴}}{{She pasted the photos into an album.}}
{{patent}}{{/ˈpætnt}}{{n./adj. 专利；明显的}}{{The company holds several patents for its inventions.}}
{{patience}}{{/ˈpeɪʃns}}{{n. 耐心；忍耐}}{{Teaching children requires great patience.}}
{{pattern}}{{/ˈpætn}}{{n. 模式；图案}}{{The pattern of behavior is hard to change.}}
{{pause}}{{/pɔːz}}{{v./n. 暂停；中断}}{{She paused for a moment before answering.}}
{{peak}}{{/piːk}}{{n./adj. 顶峰；最高的}}{{The company reached its peak in 2019.}}
{{peculiar}}{{/pɪˈkjuːliər}}{{adj. 独特的；奇怪的}}{{There was a peculiar smell in the room.}}
{{penalty}}{{/ˈpenəlti}}{{n. 惩罚；罚款}}{{The penalty for speeding is a heavy fine.}}
{{penetrate}}{{/ˈpenɪtreɪt}}{{v. 穿透；渗入}}{{The cold wind penetrated through the thin jacket.}}
{{pension}}{{/ˈpenʃn}}{{n. 养老金；退休金}}{{The government increased the pension for the elderly.}}
{{perceive}}{{/pəˈsiːv}}{{v. 察觉；理解；认为}}{{She perceived a change in his attitude.}}
{{percentage}}{{/pəˈsentɪdʒ}}{{n. 百分比；比例}}{{A large percentage of the population lives in cities.}}
{{perception}}{{/pəˈsepʃn}}{{n. 感知；认识}}{{Public perception of the company has improved.}}
{{perform}}{{/pəˈfɔːm}}{{v. 执行；表演；表现}}{{The students performed well in the exam.}}
{{permanent}}{{/ˈpɜːmənənt}}{{adj. 永久的；持久的}}{{She found a permanent job in the city.}}
{{permit}}{{/pəˈmɪt}}{{v./n. 允许；许可证}}{{Smoking is not permitted in this building.}}
{{persist}}{{/pəˈsɪst}}{{v. 坚持；持续}}{{She persisted in her efforts despite the difficulties.}}
{{personal}}{{/ˈpɜːsənl}}{{adj. 个人的；私人的}}{{Please do not ask personal questions.}}
{{perspective}}{{/pəˈspektɪv}}{{n. 观点；视角；远景}}{{Let's look at the issue from a different perspective.}}
{{persuade}}{{/pəˈsweɪd}}{{v. 说服；劝说}}{{She persuaded him to change his mind.}}
{{petroleum}}{{/pəˈtrəʊliəm}}{{n. 石油}}{{Petroleum is a major source of energy.}}
{{phase}}{{/feɪz}}{{n. 阶段；时期}}{{The project is in its final phase.}}
{{phenomenon}}{{/fɪˈnɒmɪnən}}{{n. 现象}}{{Global warming is a well-known phenomenon.}}
{{philosophy}}{{/fɪˈlɒsəfi}}{{n. 哲学；人生观}}{{He studied philosophy at university.}}
{{physical}}{{/ˈfɪzɪkl}}{{adj. 身体的；物理的}}{{Physical exercise is important for health.}}
{{pile}}{{/paɪl}}{{n./v. 堆；堆积}}{{There was a pile of books on the desk.}}
{{pilot}}{{/ˈpaɪlət}}{{n./v. 飞行员；试航}}{{The pilot landed the plane safely in bad weather.}}
{{pin}}{{/pɪn}}{{n./v. 大头针；别住}}{{She pinned the notice on the board.}}
{{pitch}}{{/pɪtʃ}}{{n./v. 球场；投掷；音调}}{{The pitcher threw the ball at high speed.}}
{{plain}}{{/pleɪn}}{{adj./n. 简单的；平原}}{{She wore a plain white dress.}}
{{plantation}}{{/plænˈteɪʃn}}{{n. 种植园}}{{The tea plantation covers hundreds of acres.}}
{{platform}}{{/ˈplætfɔːm}}{{n. 平台；站台}}{{The train arrived at platform 3.}}
{{plead}}{{/pliːd}}{{v. 恳求；辩护}}{{He pleaded not guilty in court.}}
{{pleasant}}{{/ˈpleznt}}{{adj. 令人愉快的；友好的}}{{We had a pleasant conversation over coffee.}}
{{pledge}}{{/pledʒ}}{{n./v. 誓言；保证}}{{He pledged to donate half of his wealth to charity.}}
{{plot}}{{/plɒt}}{{n./v. 情节；阴谋；策划}}{{The novel has a complicated plot.}}
{{plug}}{{/plʌɡ}}{{n./v. 插头；堵塞；宣传}}{{She plugged in the charger and waited.}}
{{plunge}}{{/plʌndʒ}}{{v./n. 跳入；骤降}}{{Stock prices plunged after the announcement.}}
{{plus}}{{/plʌs}}{{prep./n./adj. 加；优势}}{{The job requires experience plus a degree.}}
{{poison}}{{/ˈpɔɪzn}}{{n./v. 毒药；毒害}}{{The water was contaminated with poison.}}
{{policy}}{{/ˈpɒləsi}}{{n. 政策；方针}}{{The government introduced a new education policy.}}
{{polish}}{{/ˈpɒlɪʃ}}{{v./n. 擦亮；润色}}{{She polished the silver until it shone.}}
{{political}}{{/pəˈlɪtɪkl}}{{adj. 政治的}}{{Political stability is essential for economic growth.}}
{{pollution}}{{/pəˈluːʃn}}{{n. 污染}}{{Air pollution is a serious problem in many cities.}}
{{pool}}{{/puːl}}{{n. 水池；游泳池；共用资金}}{{The children were playing in the swimming pool.}}
{{popular}}{{/ˈpɒpjələr}}{{adj. 受欢迎的；流行的}}{{The song became very popular among young people.}}
{{populate}}{{/ˈpɒpjuleɪt}}{{v. 居住于；构成人口}}{{The island is populated by about 500 families.}}
{{portable}}{{/ˈpɔːtəbl}}{{adj. 便携的；手提的}}{{A portable computer is convenient for travel.}}
{{portion}}{{/ˈpɔːʃn}}{{n. 部分；一份}}{{She ate a small portion of the cake.}}
{{portrait}}{{/ˈpɔːtrɪt}}{{n. 肖像；描述}}{{The artist painted a portrait of the queen.}}
{{pose}}{{/pəʊz}}{{v./n. 摆姿势；造成；姿态}}{{The new policy poses a challenge for small businesses.}}
{{positive}}{{/ˈpɒzətɪv}}{{adj. 积极的；肯定的}}{{A positive attitude can lead to success.}}
{{possess}}{{/pəˈzes}}{{v. 拥有；具有}}{{She possesses great leadership skills.}}
{{postpone}}{{/pəʊstˈpəʊn}}{{v. 推迟；延期}}{{The meeting was postponed until next week.}}
{{potential}}{{/pəˈtenʃl}}{{adj./n. 潜在的；潜力}}{{She has the potential to become a great scientist.}}
{{pour}}{{/pɔːr}}{{v. 倒；倾泻；涌出}}{{She poured tea into the cups.}}
{{poverty}}{{/ˈpɒvəti}}{{n. 贫穷；贫困}}{{Millions of people still live in poverty.}}
{{powerful}}{{/ˈpaʊəfl}}{{adj. 强大的；有力的}}{{Knowledge is a powerful tool for change.}}
{{practical}}{{/ˈpræktɪkl}}{{adj. 实际的；实用的}}{{We need practical solutions, not just theories.}}
{{praise}}{{/preɪz}}{{v./n. 赞扬；表扬}}{{The teacher praised the student for his hard work.}}
{{pray}}{{/preɪ}}{{v. 祈祷；祈求}}{{She prayed for the safety of her family.}}
{{precious}}{{/ˈpreʃəs}}{{adj. 珍贵的；宝贵的}}{{Time is the most precious resource we have.}}
{{precise}}{{/prɪˈsaɪs}}{{adj. 精确的；准确的}}{{Please give me the precise time of the meeting.}}
{{predict}}{{/prɪˈdɪkt}}{{v. 预测；预言}}{{It is difficult to predict the future of the economy.}}
{{prefer}}{{/prɪˈfɜːr}}{{v. 更喜欢；宁愿}}{{She prefers tea to coffee.}}
{{pregnant}}{{/ˈpreɡnənt}}{{adj. 怀孕的；充满的}}{{She is pregnant with her first child.}}
{{prejudice}}{{/ˈpredʒudɪs}}{{n./v. 偏见；歧视}}{{Prejudice against minorities is still a problem.}}
{{preliminary}}{{/prɪˈlɪmɪnəri}}{{adj./n. 初步的；预备的}}{{The preliminary results are encouraging.}}
{{premise}}{{/ˈpremɪs}}{{n. 前提；房屋}}{{The argument is based on a false premise.}}
{{prepare}}{{/prɪˈpeər}}{{v. 准备；预备}}{{She prepared a delicious meal for the guests.}}
{{prescribe}}{{/prɪˈskraɪb}}{{v. 开处方；规定}}{{The doctor prescribed a new medicine for the patient.}}
{{presence}}{{/ˈprezns}}{{n. 存在；出席；风度}}{{His presence at the meeting was greatly appreciated.}}
{{preserve}}{{/prɪˈzɜːv}}{{v. 保护；保存；保持}}{{We must preserve our cultural heritage.}}
{{press}}{{/pres}}{{v./n. 按；压；新闻界}}{{The journalist works for the national press.}}
{{pressure}}{{/ˈpreʃər}}{{n. 压力；压迫}}{{Students are under a lot of pressure during exams.}}
{{prestige}}{{/preˈstiːʒ}}{{n. 威望；声望}}{{The university enjoys international prestige.}}
{{presume}}{{/prɪˈzjuːm}}{{v. 假定；认为}}{{I presume you have read the report.}}
{{pretend}}{{/prɪˈtend}}{{v. 假装；佯装}}{{He pretended to be asleep when I entered the room.}}
{{prevail}}{{/prɪˈveɪl}}{{v. 盛行；获胜；说服}}{{Justice will prevail in the end.}}
{{prevent}}{{/prɪˈvent}}{{v. 预防；阻止}}{{Washing hands regularly can prevent the spread of disease.}}
{{previous}}{{/ˈpriːviəs}}{{adj. 以前的；先的}}{{She had no previous experience in management.}}
{{pride}}{{/praɪd}}{{n. 骄傲；自豪}}{{She takes pride in her work.}}
{{primary}}{{/ˈpraɪməri}}{{adj. 主要的；初级的}}{{Education is the primary concern for most parents.}}
{{primitive}}{{/ˈprɪmɪtɪv}}{{adj. 原始的；简陋的}}{{Primitive people lived in caves.}}
{{principle}}{{/ˈprɪnsəpl}}{{n. 原则；原理}}{{He is a man of principle.}}
{{prior}}{{/ˈpraɪər}}{{adj. 在前的；优先的}}{{Prior to the meeting, please read the report.}}
{{priority}}{{/praɪˈɒrəti}}{{n. 优先；优先事项}}{{Safety is our top priority.}}
{{privilege}}{{/ˈprɪvəlɪdʒ}}{{n. 特权；荣幸}}{{Education is a right, not a privilege.}}
{{probe}}{{/prəʊb}}{{v./n. 探索；调查；探测器}}{{Scientists sent a space probe to Mars.}}
{{proceed}}{{/prəˈsiːd}}{{v. 继续；进行}}{{Please proceed to the next question.}}
{{process}}{{/ˈprəʊses}}{{n./v. 过程；加工；处理}}{{The process of learning takes time and effort.}}
{{proclaim}}{{/prəˈkleɪm}}{{v. 宣布；声明}}{{The president proclaimed a state of emergency.}}
{{produce}}{{/prəˈdjuːs}}{{v./n. 生产；产品}}{{The factory produces electronic devices.}}
{{profession}}{{/prəˈfeʃn}}{{n. 职业；行业}}{{Teaching is a noble profession.}}
{{proficient}}{{/prəˈfɪʃnt}}{{adj. 熟练的；精通的}}{{She is proficient in both English and French.}}
{{profit}}{{/ˈprɒfɪt}}{{n./v. 利润；获益}}{{The company made a large profit this year.}}
{{profound}}{{/prəˈfaʊnd}}{{adj. 深刻的；深远的}}{{The book had a profound impact on my thinking.}}
{{program}}{{/ˈprəʊɡræm}}{{n. 程序；节目；计划}}{{The government launched a new training program.}}
{{progress}}{{/ˈprəʊɡres}}{{n./v. 进步；进展}}{{She has made great progress in her studies.}}
{{prohibit}}{{/prəˈhɪbɪt}}{{v. 禁止；阻止}}{{The law prohibits the sale of alcohol to minors.}}
{{project}}{{/ˈprɒdʒekt}}{{n./v. 项目；投射；预计}}{{The construction project will take two years to complete.}}
{{prominent}}{{/ˈprɒmɪnənt}}{{adj. 突出的；著名的}}{{She is a prominent figure in the field of medicine.}}
{{promote}}{{/prəˈməʊt}}{{v. 促进；晋升；推销}}{{The company promoted him to senior manager.}}
{{prompt}}{{/prɒmpt}}{{adj./v. 迅速的；促使}}{{The news prompted a public debate.}}
{{proof}}{{/pruːf}}{{n. 证据；证明}}{{There is no proof that he committed the crime.}}
{{proper}}{{/ˈprɒpər}}{{adj. 适当的；正确的}}{{Please wear proper attire for the occasion.}}
{{property}}{{/ˈprɒpəti}}{{n. 财产；房地产；性质}}{{The property market has been booming.}}
{{proportion}}{{/prəˈpɔːʃn}}{{n. 比例；部分}}{{A large proportion of the budget goes to education.}}
{{propose}}{{/prəˈpəʊz}}{{v. 提议；建议；求婚}}{{He proposed a new plan for the project.}}
{{prospect}}{{/ˈprɒspekt}}{{n. 前景；展望}}{{The job offers good career prospects.}}
{{prosperity}}{{/prɒˈsperəti}}{{n. 繁荣；兴旺}}{{The country enjoyed a period of prosperity.}}
{{protect}}{{/prəˈtekt}}{{v. 保护；防护}}{{Sunscreen protects your skin from UV rays.}}
{{protest}}{{/ˈprəʊtest}}{{n./v. 抗议；反对}}{{Thousands joined the protest against the new law.}}
{{prove}}{{/pruːv}}{{v. 证明；证实}}{{The experiment proved the theory correct.}}
{{provide}}{{/prəˈvaɪd}}{{v. 提供；供应}}{{The hotel provides free Wi-Fi for guests.}}
{{provoke}}{{/prəˈvəʊk}}{{v. 激怒；引起}}{{His remarks provoked anger among the audience.}}
{{psychological}}{{/ˌsaɪkəˈlɒdʒɪkl}}{{adj. 心理的；心理学的}}{{The event had a deep psychological impact on the survivors.}}
{{publication}}{{/ˌpʌblɪˈkeɪʃn}}{{n. 出版物；出版}}{{The publication of the book was delayed.}}
{{publish}}{{/ˈpʌblɪʃ}}{{v. 出版；发表}}{{The journal published her research paper.}}
{{punish}}{{/ˈpʌnɪʃ}}{{v. 惩罚；处罚}}{{The law punishes those who break the rules.}}
{{purchase}}{{/ˈpɜːtʃəs}}{{v./n. 购买；购置}}{{She purchased a new laptop online.}}
{{pure}}{{/pjʊər}}{{adj. 纯的；纯洁的}}{{The water in the mountain stream is very pure.}}
{{purpose}}{{/ˈpɜːpəs}}{{n. 目的；用途}}{{The purpose of the meeting is to discuss the budget.}}
{{pursue}}{{/pəˈsjuː}}{{v. 追求；追赶；从事}}{{She pursued a career in medicine.}}
{{puzzle}}{{/ˈpʌzl}}{{n./v. 谜；困惑}}{{The mystery puzzled the police for months.}}
